From 3a42a0ce8d9c399a10906c8f059db01d65ec85d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:21:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] antinomie: record task credentials and hash executed and
 deleted files

Write each traced task's credentials (uid, euid, suid, fsuid, the gid
equivalents, the audit login uid and session, and all five capability sets
with the securebits) as a lifecycle record, layout antinomie.creds/2 (96
bytes), at its first traced call and after every change, from one hook in
commit_creds() plus the loginuid setter. Changes to the ambient and bounding
sets and to the securebits (prctl) are recorded with reason PRCTL.

A worker hashes (SHA-256) the image an exec committed and the file an unlink
removed, through a private read-only open with no notification and no
access-time update, from a bounded queue and size budget, and publishes the
result or the reason it was skipped under the originating call's identity. The
call records the file's state (inode identity, size, modification and change
time, and the change counter, which is armed when it is read); the worker
compares all of it with the state after the read and sets CHANGED on any
difference. For a delete, the state is taken again after the unlink, which
itself moves the change time; a queued or running job whose file matched its
state just before a traced task unlinks it (a sample that executes itself and
deletes its image) takes the post-unlink state, so the delete does not read as
a write. The digest is the bytes at hashing time, never at the call. The
digest cache is keyed on the same state, is bounded by a monotonic age, and is
used only on filesystems that keep a change counter (ext4, tmpfs), because
coarse timestamps cannot tell a rewrite within one tick apart. A worker that
cannot publish skips the read and counts the loss.
---
 fs/exec.c                         |   2 +-
 fs/namei.c                        |   4 +
 include/linux/antinomie_monitor.h |  22 +-
 kernel/antinomie/Kconfig          |   1 +
 kernel/antinomie/Makefile         |   1 +
 kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h   |  55 +++-
 kernel/antinomie/hash.c           | 520 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel/antinomie/hash.h           |  11 +
 kernel/antinomie/notes.h          |  27 ++
 kernel/antinomie/recorder.c       | 200 +++++++++++-
 kernel/audit.c                    |   2 +
 kernel/cred.c                     |   3 +
 12 files changed, 843 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 kernel/antinomie/hash.c
 create mode 100644 kernel/antinomie/hash.h
 create mode 100644 kernel/antinomie/notes.h

